<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">August Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The August Revolution was the seizure of power across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> in August 1945, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s surrender at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Uprisings took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> on 19 August, Hue and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> soon after, and Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bảo Đại</a> abdicated on 30 August. On 2 September <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> proclaimed the Democratic Republic of Vietnam, opening the conflict with returning French forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/august-revolution.jpg" alt="August Revolution" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vũ Năng An · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%C3%A1ch_m%E1%BA%A1ng_th%C3%A1ng_8_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
